:-) I'm not surprised.  I chased around and around that barn as well. 
What's really annoying is that the information given on the
digital/Compaq/HP site is wrong as well!  Here's my super simple,
can't be patented, instructions:

In this place

   ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v6.4/alphapc164lx/

download the "lx164srm.rom" file, put it alone on a DOS floppy, and
use the AlphaBIOS console "Firmware Update" menu item.  If your floppy
is good, it will load up and reprogram the flash with the new SRM
image.  I can't remember if the machine reboots or gives you
instructions to reboot.  In either case, reboot the machine *at the
right time* and you'll then boot into a bright, Digital blue screen
(which looks frighteningly close to the blue screen of death).  You
will see a series of hexadecimal digits print out on the top of the
screen and then within a few tens of seconds, you'll get the SRM
prompt.


