I suspect that this is the same problem I had with my MiataGL. I put 
printk statements and found that it was locking when it calls es1888_init()
in linux/arch/alpha/kernel/sys_miata.c. My solution was to comment out
that line and build the kernel on a non-GL Miata where it didn't have this
problem, and then do a complete system disk-to-disk transfer. (This was in
the last two weeks or so.) I communicated with someone else who had posted
of the problem in December, and he emailed Debian asking them if they 
could create a new boot kernel that didn't include that probe. YOu might
email them and ask them also. I could also email you a kernel image that
I compiled, although I don't know how to make one that would work with
Debian install.


