I put a bunch of printk statements in the kernel code and recompiled, and
it turns out it was locking when probing for the ES1888 sound chip. I worked
around it by editing the kernel file linux/arch/alpha/kernel/sys_miata.c,
and commented out the line

        es1888_init();

This gave me a bootable kernel.  I was then able to do a disk-to-disk 
transfer of the system from one of the other Miata's I have (no GL) and
get it running. I have no idea what it was actually hitting that locked
the system, but as I don't care about sound this is a very good result.


