OK and here's already the problem: Your kernel doesn't recognise your SCSI
adapter. The installer placed a initrd image in sda1:/boot which will very
likely include the needed driver.
Unfortunately, AFAIK MILO can't handle seperate (i.e. not the same file as
the kernel) initrds and there's no SRM available for XL and XLTs.

If you can get this to boot, maybe with the installation disks, you can
build your own kernel with all nessecary drivers included.

One other thing woth a try: I noticed there're MILOs out there which don't
know about symlinks, so you might try

  boot sda1:/boot/vmlinux-2.4.9-32.5 root=/dev/sda1

you might also try to use root=/dev/ram and/or load_ramdisk=1 parameters.

One last thing out of personal interest: How much memory does your XLT have?

