If you still have a manual for your monitor, follow the troubleshooting
instructions in the back. If not, try some of these:

The power cord often becomes loose from the back of the monitor yet looks
and feels plugged in correctly. Try unplugging it and firmly plug it back
in.

Try the same with all other cables.

The video card may be loose. You will have to open the box, remove the video
card and plug it back in.

Many computers have a video card built into the MB and another higher
resolution card. If your computer has multiple monitor ports, try another.

If the monitor was bumped sharply during the relocation, it is possible that
it has resulted in a blown picture tube. If so, throw it away and buy a new
one.

